  "notes": "KANJI DISTINCTION:\nThe verb さす has multiple kanji depending on meaning:\n- {射|さ}す: to shine (light strikes/enters)\n- ⟦{刺|さ}す→刺す：02111_sasu⟧: to stab, pierce\n- ⟦{指|さ}す→指す：02056_sasu⟧: to point at\n- ⟦{差|さ}す→差す：17637_sasu⟧: to hold up (umbrella), to pour\n- ⟦{挿|さ}す→挿す：02466_sasu⟧: to insert\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- No standard transitive pair\n- Pattern: {射|さ}す\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{日|ひ}→日：02249_hi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{射|さ}す: sunlight shines in\n- ⟦{光|ひかり}→光：01707_hikari⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{射|さ}す: light shines through\n- ⟦{西日|にしび}→西日：27853_nishibi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{射|さ}す: afternoon sun shines in\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\n{射|さ}す describes light entering or falling on a surface. Often used in poetic or descriptive contexts about natural lighting.",
